Assets of the vis-buffer golden scenes (tests/golden/visbuffer/, DENG-240)
==========================================================================

The scenes use no asset files. Every mesh, material and texture is generated by the scene code at
run time, so there is nothing to licence: all of them are original procedural data of this
repository (the same licence as the code).

| Asset                 | Made by (vis_golden.c)  | What it is                                              |
|-----------------------|-------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| box                   | vg_mesh_box             | six faces, each an n x n quad grid, outward normals     |
| UV sphere             | vg_mesh_sphere          | `seg` segments x `seg / 2` rings, no triangles at poles |
| plane                 | vg_mesh_plane           | an n x n quad grid in XY facing +Z (ground)             |
| card                  | vg_mesh_card            | an n x n quad grid in XZ facing -Y (cutouts)            |
| checker texture       | vg_material_cutout      | 8 x 8 RGBA8, alpha alternating 255 / 0                  |
| materials             | vg_material             | flat base colours, roughness 0.5, opaque or mask        |

Meshes are written as glTF 2.0 in memory (positions, normals, UV0, 32-bit indices in a base64
data-URI buffer) and cooked through the S11 model importer exactly as `de-cook` would cook a
`.gltf` file: the glTF front end (tools/cook/importers/model/gltf_import.c), the glTF-to-engine
axis conversion, and the DMSH v2 mesh stage (LOD chain, vertex quantization, meshlets with
cones; mesh_cook.c, mesh_lod.c, mesh_quantize.c, mesh_meshlets.c). The cooked blob is then placed
in GPU buffers with the layout of the runtime mesh loader.

Should a scene ever need an asset file, it goes in this directory with its source and licence
in this table (CC0 or generated only).
